// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Soldier 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1213129879" "It doesn't take much training or expertise to join the 5th Column. Members who have neither receive basic weapons and are immediately put into service in the ranks of the Nebel, the 5th Column's front-line ranks. After all, the 5th Column believes in survival of the fittest."
// DisplayNames :
"P3311684263" "Nebel Rifle"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Soldier_Missle 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1892424638" "Nebel Rocket"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Soldier_Grenade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3163043321" "Nebel Grenade"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Soldier_Flamethrower 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1494402754" "Nebel Fire"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Soldier_Chaingun 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3923260250" "Nebel Force"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Soldier_Martial_Arts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3985125180" "As far as the 5th Column's concerned, the best way to prove one's worthiness is to survive and blossom in the crucible of combat. The 5th Column Martial Artists are good at doing just that. They are the best soldiers in their squads, and they're not above pointing this out to their comrades."
// DisplayNames :
"P716822385" "Nebel Fist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Soldier_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1917917851" "Only those Nebel Soldiers who have proven both resilient and trustworthy achieve the rank of Unteroffizier, or 'underofficer.' Through their skill in combat and their dedication to the 5th Column's cause, they have begun to earn real respect from their masters. In return, they receive better equipment and training, and are trusted with some low level secrets."
// DisplayNames :
"P312715925" "Nebel Unteroffizier"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Soldier_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1860127211" "To be commissioned an Oberst, or Colonel, a Nebel soldier must prove himself over the course of many battles. Many of them resent having to continue working with raw recruits, but this indignity is more than compensated for by their first taste of super soldier serums and body enhancements. Combined with their combat experience, these enhancements make them formidable foes."
// DisplayNames :
"P487636158" "Nebel Oberst"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Elite 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2642190992" "Once a soldier has proven his total commitment to the cause, he is transferred into the ranks of the Elite. Only one in five soldiers survive long enough to achieve this promotion. Nebel Elites receive first stage super soldier serum that improves their physical prowess to the level of Olympic athletes. They also go through training courses before being put back into the battle lines. After all, the 5th Column has made an investment in their success."
// DisplayNames :
"P773860443" "Nebel Elite Rifle"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Elite_Missle 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Elite_Grenade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Elite_Flamethrower 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Elite_Chaingun 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Elite_Martial_Arts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Elite_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1943625014" "A high-ranking Nebel Elite Unteroffizier is a force to be reckoned with. His increased physical prowess is now matched by improved tactical skills and the steely resolve of a combat veteran. The super soldier serum and attendant propaganda have left the soldier utterly devoted to the 5th Column's cause. He is willing to follow any order, and he seldom worries about the messy consequences."
// DisplayNames :
"P2580311291" "Nebel Elite Unteroffizier"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Elite_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1291294377" "The leaders of the Nebel Elite are near perfect soldierly specimens. In addition to the normal super soldier serum, they receive a special formula that enhances intellect and problem solving skills. An Elite Oberst is utterly devoted to the 5th Column's cause, and he can finally be trusted to lead his soldiers without direction from above."
// DisplayNames :
"P2851096303" "Nebel Elite Oberst"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Ubermenschen_Thug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P796686584" "An Ubermensch, or 'Over Man' is a 5th Column soldier who has undergone a long and painful regimen of super soldier treatments. The Nebel Ubermenschen are the most numerous of these medical marvels, but that doesn't mean they're common. They've had extensive training and thousands of dollars worth of drugs pumped into them. It's an investment that usually pays off, since a first rank Ubermensch is stronger than five normal men."
// DisplayNames :
"P3002442381" "Nebel Ubermenschen Rifle"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Ubermenschen_Missle 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2868921216" "Nebel Ubermenschen Rocket"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Ubermenschen_Grenade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2100487178" "Nebel Ubermenschen Grenade"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Ubermenschen_Flamethrower 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3486153411" "Nebel Ubermenschen Fire"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Ubermenschen_Chaingun 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2655640432" "Nebel Ubermenschen Force"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Ubermenschen_Martial_Arts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3160501104" "Nebel Ubermenschen Fist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Ubermenschen_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1144325783" "The pinnacle of frontline soldiers, the Ubermenschen Unteroffizier are nearly unstoppable fighting machines. It often takes an anti-tank weapon just to faze one of these juggernauts. Fortunately, their numbers are small, though the 5th Column keeps making more of them as their soldiers become more experienced."
// DisplayNames :
"P3616720194" "Nebel Ubermenschen Unteroffizier"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fog_Ubermenschen_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1823268373" "The highest ranking soldiers among the Nebel, the Nebel Ubermenschen Obersts are strikingly capable field officers, able to formulate and execute grand military campaigns. Unlike most modern officers, these Ubermenschen are not afraid to personally lead their soldiers into battle. After all, their own abilities far surpass those of all normal men and many super-powered heroes."
// DisplayNames :
"P3336365184" "Nebel Ubermenschen Oberst"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Soldier 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P741172371" "The Nacht is the 5th Column's special operations division, tasked with covert ops, assassinations, and espionage. Even the lowest level recruits receive some special training, particularly in stealth and evasion techniques. New recruits must have some military or law enforcement experience before being accepted into the Nacht."
// DisplayNames :
"P348142054" "Nacht Rifle"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Soldier_Missle 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1908854475" "Nacht Rocket"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Soldier_Grenade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2632366751" "Nacht Grenade"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Soldier_Flamethrower 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1174828646" "Nacht Fire"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Soldier_Chaingun 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P947666971" "Nacht Force"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Soldier_Martial_Arts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P900556757" "Nacht Fist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Soldier_Martial_Arts_Variant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Soldier_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1593569870" "The Nacht Unteroffizier have completed their covert ops training and are on the verge of being promoted to Elite status. They have yet to benefit from a course of super soldier serum, but they have honed their stealth and physique to a near perfect level. Unteroffizier are often tasked with leading squads of Nacht soldiers on raids to raise funds for the 5th Column."
// DisplayNames :
"P470591297" "Nacht Unteroffizier"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Soldier_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2310520631" "A Nacht Oberst is responsible for overseeing squads of covert operatives. Since coverts ops need to be precise and perfectly executed, a Nacht Oberst is valued chiefly for his ability to follow orders precisely and make sure his troops do the same. In return for loyalty and good service, Obersts receive their first taste of super soldier serum, making them stronger and quicker than any normal human could be."
// DisplayNames :
"P471493067" "Nacht Oberst"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Elite 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P344711891" "The Nacht Elites are world-class special forces operatives, as well trained as any Navy SEAL. They're expert insurgents, capable of infiltrating a target swiftly and silently, then taking it down. Elites undergo a basic super soldier regimen designed to heighten their stealth, accuracy, and concentration. These enhancements make them incredibly dangerous, especially when encountered in force."
// DisplayNames :
"P437567192" "Nacht Elite Rifle"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Elite_Missle 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2963867623" "Nacht Elite Rocket"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Elite_Grenade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2935994805" "Nacht Elite Grenade"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Elite_Flamethrower 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1225357934" "Nacht Elite Fire"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Elite_Chaingun 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P917030693" "Nacht Elite Force"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Elite_Martial_Arts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P983722973" "Nacht Elite Fist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Elite_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P731011146" "A Nacht Elite at the peak of his game may earn the rank of Unteroffizier, and with it a large upgrade in super soldier serum. He is on the verge of Ubermensch status, and his mind has become focused with laser-like intensity. High ranking Elites are some of the best shots and most dedicated insurgents in the world. They can, and have, assassinated heads of state as well as world famous heroes."
// DisplayNames :
"P4150645290" "Nacht Elite Unteroffizier"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Elite_Sniper 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2955552461" "Those gifted with incredible accuracy are quickly transferred into the Nacht division, where they undergo lengthy treatments to refine their abilities. The Sharpshooters are natural loners and disdain associating with the rank and file. The only praise they seek is the satisfaction of a silent kill."
// DisplayNames :
"P3549644716" "Nacht Elite Sharpshooter"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Elite_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3213699915" "While most Elites concentrate on learning the basic skills required for special ops, the Obersts receive additional training in tactics. They're also trained in technological skills, such as wire tapping and circumventing security systems. Combined with their prodigious super soldier enhancements, these skills make Elite Obersts well-prepared to plan and carry out small covert ops."
// DisplayNames :
"P3715473639" "Nacht Elite Oberst"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Elite_Boss_Lycanthrope 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Ubermenschen 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3029037400" "The Ubermenschen of the Nacht have transcended mere special ops status. They are each unto themselves a powerful covert force, capable of taking on operations that would normally require an entire team of commandos. In addition to their enhanced physical and mental attributes, they receive training in security systems, computer infiltration, and surveillance equipment. In many ways, they are the perfect spies."
// DisplayNames :
"P1884132378" "Nacht Ubermenschen Rifle"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Ubermenschen_Missle 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3316251985" "Nacht Ubermenschen Rocket"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Ubermenschen_Grenade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2357768182" "Nacht Ubermenschen Grenade"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Ubermenschen_Flamethrower 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2684570239" "Nacht Ubermenschen Fire"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Ubermenschen_Chaingun 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1559358951" "Nacht Ubermenschen Force"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Ubermenschen_Martial_Arts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3551026124" "Nacht Ubermenschen Fist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Ubermenschen_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3806343464" "Unlike their counterparts in the other branches of the 5th Column hierarchy, the Nacht Ubermenschen Unteroffizier have considerable autonomy. The 5th Column feels that the subversive activities that fall within the Nacht's purview require a certain amount of independence. This makes the Nacht Ubermenschen quite unpredictable at times - and thus, quite deadly."
// DisplayNames :
"P1546175073" "Nacht Ubermenschen Unteroffizier"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Ubermenschen_Lycanthrope_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Night_Ubermenschen_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4229563297" "The Nacht Ubermenschen Obersts author their own plans to sow terror and fear across Paragon City. Many are in command of small military cells, completely cut off from their compatriots - both for the sake of security, and to encourage independent thinking."
// DisplayNames :
"P2826263121" "Nacht Ubermenschen Oberst"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Soldier 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P143346825" "The Raserei are the pride and joy of the 5th Column's army. They represent the ideal to which all other followers of the cause should aspire. Not only are they disciplined, well-trained soldiers; they're also perfect students of the fascist beliefs that form the core of the 5th Column's ideology. Only those who have proven both their ability and loyalty are permitted to join the ranks of the Raserei."
// DisplayNames :
"P1722840153" "Raserei Rifle"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Soldier_Missle 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P711594139" "Raserei Rocket"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Soldier_Grenade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P4158015413" "Raserei Grenade"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Soldier_Flamethrower 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P824986784" "Raserei Fire"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Soldier_Chaingun 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1242303908" "Raserei Force"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Soldier_Martial_Arts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1116167443" "Raserei Fist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Soldier_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4108600229" "Raserei Unteroffizier are zealots in every sense of the word. They believe in the 5th Column creed so fiercely that they have become experts at recruiting new members from the disaffected elements of society. Raserei Unteroffizier are in equal parts soldier and proselytizer."
// DisplayNames :
"P3191261597" "Raserei Unteroffizier"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Soldier_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4122482940" "The Raserei Obersts are the living essence of the 5th Column beliefs. While the Unteroffizier brim with enthusiasm, the Obersts radiate a palpable aura of danger. The Raserei carefully foster this mystique in order to keep order within the ranks of the 5th Column."
// DisplayNames :
"P1203156891" "Raserei Oberst"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Elite 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1317246656" "Elite members of the Raserei have not only proven their loyalty to the cause, they've also shown themselves capable of bringing new members into the fold. Only those who have achieved Elite status are allowed to interact directly with potential recruits. Their fanatical devotion ensures that they'll either convert the potential member, or kill him. Either way, the secrets of the 5th Column remain secure."
// DisplayNames :
"P1839308578" "Raserei Elite Rifle"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Elite_Missle 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3988171204" "Raserei Elite Rocket"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Elite_Grenade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P214292329" "Raserei Elite Grenade"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Elite_Flamethrower 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P4212659823" "Raserei Elite Fire"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Elite_Chaingun 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1092478687" "Raserei Elite Force"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Elite_Martial_Arts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2293434332" "Raserei Elite Fist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Elite_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2437281098" "The Elite Raserei Unteroffizier are those destined for positions of authority in the 5th Column hierarchy. Their authority supercedes nearly every other rank. These Unteroffizier reward the 5th Column with fanatical devotion to the cause. By the time someone has reached this lofty level, they have given up any semblance of a normal life. They belong to the Column, body and soul."
// DisplayNames :
"P4059125401" "Raserei Elite Unteroffizier"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Elite_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1923996907" "The Raserei Elite Obersts are among the few soldiers permitted to express their opinions to the 5th Column's leaders, though most wisely avoid doing so. They control almost all the internal operations of the 5th Column organization."
// DisplayNames :
"P2154434244" "Raserei Elite Oberst"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Ubermenschen 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2475649810" "Every member of the 5th Column aspires to become one of the Raserei Ubermenschen, but few of them achieve this lofty goal. They are the spiritual and philosophical leaders of the 5th Column - totally devoted to its beliefs and goals. Like any good soldier, they lead by example. Their intense training and physical enhancements make them perfect soldiers and perfect models of behavior. In battle, they serve as an inspiration to all who fight at their side."
// DisplayNames :
"P1383872607" "Raserei Ubermenschen Rifle"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Ubermenschen_Missle 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3275586018" "Raserei Ubermenschen Rocket"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Ubermenschen_Grenade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3739670852" "Raserei Ubermenschen Grenade"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Ubermenschen_Flamethrower 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2478421705" "Raserei Ubermenschen Fire"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Ubermenschen_Chaingun 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2126528930" "Raserei Ubermenschen Force"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Ubermenschen_Martial_Arts 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3759318906" "Raserei Ubermenschen Fist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Ubermenschen_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1310230690" "Raserei Ubermenschen Unteroffiziere have the responsibility of leading large numbers of troops. They are concerned with training their men into peak fighting form - and recruiting new members to the cause. Until recently, none have ever been taken alive by the authorities."
// DisplayNames :
"P3380158366" "Raserei Ubermenschen Unteroffizier"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fury_Ubermenschen_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P881588267" "The Raserei Ubermenschen Obersts make up the inner circle that surrounds the 5th Column leadership. They are charged with the grand stratagems that further the ultimate goal of the 5th Column: the eventual domination of the world. The leaders of the Column foster a competitiveness between these high ranking officers in order to prevent any single one of them from acquiring too much power and becoming a threat."
// DisplayNames :
"P2934038242" "Raserei Ubermenschen Oberst"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fifth_Mek_Man 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1234408291" "Vandal, the genius behind the 5th Column's technology, created the first Mek Men during World War II. He's been improving on them ever since. The tough and deadly versions in operation today are 100 times more dangerous than their predecessors of 60 years ago. Modern Mek Men have tough, thick armor, redundant systems that resist damage, and a powerful onboard AI that makes them faster and smarter than most human soldiers."
// DisplayNames :
"P16233574" "Mek Man"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fifth_Hoverbot 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1955717623" "The Steel Valkyrie class Hoverbot is one of the 5th Column's more ingenious inventions. Rumor has it that Vandal was inspired by the Rikti attack drones, but there have been versions of the Valkyrie in service since WWII. Mounted with omni-directional jets and banks of armor piercing rockets, the Steel Valkyries are quite maneuverable and pack a deadly punch. They can make the skies a very dangerous place."
// DisplayNames :
"P3476939984" "Steel Valkyrie"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fifth_Nightwolf 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1649882118" "The nature of the Nightwolves remains a terrifying mystery. These monstrous, werewolf like creatures were once human beings, but they have since been warped beyond all recognition. Unlike the Vampyri, these beasts are not the result of any known super serum treatment. Many suspect that some kind of magic is involved in their transformation."
// DisplayNames :
"P1105410566" "Nightwolf"
// DisplayNames :
"P2512800327" "Darkwolf"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fifth_Nightwolf_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P827648241" "The Nightwolf Champion has lost all of his humanity to whatever force transformed him into a monstrous killing machine. Unlike the more sedate Nightwolf warriors, the Champions are in a wild state and can barely be controlled. They are berserkers, unwilling to obey any orders when their enemy is in sight. They are, however, nearly impossible to kill, which makes up for their disobedient nature."
// DisplayNames :
"P749995770" "Nightwolf Champion"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Lt_Nightwolf_Lycan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1231432022" "Some Nightwolves have mastered the ability to temporarily transform back into their human body. This allows these soldiers to infiltrate targeted facilities before revealing their monstrous nature. The authorities have little time to react once they realize what they're dealing with."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Boss_Nightwolf 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3572735420" "The Warwolf has lost all of his humanity to whatever force transformed him into a monstrous killing machine. Unlike the more sedate Nightwolf warriors, the Warwolves are in a wild state and can barely be controlled. They are berserkers, unwilling to obey any orders when their enemy is in sight. They are, however, nearly impossible to kill, which makes up for their disobedient nature."
// DisplayNames :
"P3814626281" "Warwolf"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Boss_Nightwolf_Lycan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fifth_Vampyr_Life_Drain 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P872504620" "The Vampyri are not true vampires at all. They are instead the ultimate result of the 5th Column's super soldier program. It takes a full year of chemical treatments and surgical enhancements to create a single Vampyr, but the result is one of the most deadly killing machines in the world. All Vampyri have incredible strength, speed, and resilience. The Vampyr Parasite has the ability to drain life from its targets, while strengthening itself."
// DisplayNames :
"P546131332" "Vampyr Parasite"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fifth_Vampyr_Mesmerist 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1206486178" "The Vampyri are not true vampires at all. They are instead the ultimate result of the 5th Column's super soldier program. It takes a full year of chemical treatments and surgical enhancements to create a single Vampyr, but the result is one of the most deadly killing machines in the world. All Vampyri have incredible strength, speed, and resilience. The Vampyr Mesmerist has potent hypnotic abilities that entrance enemies and render them helpless."
// DisplayNames :
"P120702855" "Vampyr Mesmerist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fifth_Vampyr_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P457838272" "The Vampyri Adjutants are soldiers who have been promoted from the Ubermenschen ranks and given the singular honor of becoming a Vampyr. This honor is one the masters of the 5th Column are loathe to give, since it means a year of inactive duty for the Ubermensch. The result, however, is a Vampyr who has both the power and the experience to lead his monstrous soldiers into battle."
// DisplayNames :
"P4044902666" "Vampyr Adjutant"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fifth_Vampyr_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1565267706" "The Vampyri Commandants are the assistants to Nosferatu, the man responsible for the 5th Column's super soldier program. Commandants are scientists as well as super soldiers, and have a hand in the creation of other Vampyri. They often personalize their own transformation process, giving themselves special abilities and powers that lesser beings can only dream of."
// DisplayNames :
"P1996720469" "Vampyr Commandant"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fifth_Dark_Vampyr_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1792307864" "The Dark Vampyri are the assistants to Nosferatu, the man responsible for the 5th Column's super soldier program. Commandants are scientists as well as super soldiers, and have a hand in the creation of other Vampyri. They often personalize their own transformation process, giving themselves special abilities and powers that lesser beings can only dream of."
// DisplayNames :
"P211090139" "Dark Vampyr"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fifth_Wolfpack_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2725995812" "The Mk I Wolfpack robot has been favorably compared to a battle tank when it comes to both firepower and resilience. The big difference is that the Mk I is controlled by an ingenious artificial intelligence that can capably command troops in the field. It carries enough firepower to take out heavily armored targets, and its own armor stands up to anything less than an anti-tank weapon."
// DisplayNames :
"P1644808757" "Mk I Wolfpack robot"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fifth_Wolfpack_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P504361608" "The ultimate in automated fighting systems, the Mk II Wolfpack robot is fearsome in combat, capable of taking on whole armored companies by itself. The robots' unerring aim and large caliber weaponry make them a threat to any hero they come across. Their enhanced AI allows them to coordinate with the 5th Column's human troops, making them the perfect battlefield commanders."
// DisplayNames :
"P3660354486" "Mk II Wolfpack robot"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Requiem 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3307726576" "Ridolfo Uzzano has come a long way from his humble beginning as one of Mussolini's lapdogs. The primary cause of his success was his fusion with a Nictus, a being of utter darkness. The Nictus gave Ridolfo the ability to scorch his foes with an infernal fire. Though he is now over 100 years old, Requiem remains a fearsome foe in battle."
// DisplayNames :
"P2244170352" "Requiem"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Requiem_EB_Low 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Vandal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2399842355" "The fiend known as Vandal was once a humble tinkerer named Othman Doul. In the late 1930's, the villain Requiem recognized Doul's usefulness and recruited him to the nascent 5th Column. Othman was happy to oblige, since it meant he could indulge his scientific curiosity without restraint. Over the years, Vandal has mechanically augmented himself to prolong his lifespan. Now, he seeks to advance his own position within the 5th Column and perhaps even challenge Requiem for supremacy."
// DisplayNames :
"P1669497069" "Vandal"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Nosferatu 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3019526964" "Few truly appreciate the genius of Nosferatu's super soldier program, and none more so than himself. Nosferatu was so entranced by his ability to create the super strong Vampyri that he became one of them. He has since improved upon his original design by granting himself several new abilities. He can mesmerize his opponents, leaving them helpless. Some say he can even siphon off the life force of his foes."
// DisplayNames :
"P1215451297" "Nosferatu"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Schadenfreude 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1367988556" "Schadenfreude has remained loyal to the 5th Column cause and has risen to a high rank within the resurgent organization."
// DisplayNames :
"P1307786031" "Schadenfreude"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Door 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1317399436" "This reinforced door stands between you and freedom!  The door seems to be vibrate and hum, as though it is coursing with energy."
// DisplayClassName :
"P2936123098" "Object"
// DisplayNames :
"P699576872" "Reinforced Door"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Dampening_Field 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P632564129" "Dampening Field"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Gladiator 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1332548465" "After the Council took over, this soldier found himself suddenly unemployed. He now works for those he chooses worthy, waiting to recall the true glory of the 5th Column."
// DisplayNames :
"P2847078306" "5th Column Krieger"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Archon_Burkholder 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P818344873" "Archon Burkholder has made a name for himself in the 5th Column. His obsession with robotics led him to carve off his own arm and replace it with one of steel; it also led him to create a terrifying robot factory. There is nearly nothing Burkholder won't do to achieve his own ends."
// DisplayNames :
"P3920060084" "Archon Burkholder"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Maestro 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2012593601" "As a child, Vincenzo Alferi dreamed of becoming a great composer, but those dreams were shattered when he lost his hearing due to a car accident. The 5th Column offered to perform a radical experiment that might restore his hearing, and Vincenzo agreed without hesitation. Unfortunately, things did not go as planned. An Arachnos attack on the facility resulted in a power surge at the worst possible moment. Instead of restoring him, the resulting explosion created a permanent resonance in Vincenzo's body. He agreed to join the 5th Column if they would give him the opportunity for vengeance against Arachnos."
// DisplayNames :
"P3233564486" "Maestro"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Reichsman_V 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4253524737" "This Marcus Cole, from an alternate dimension, was a rogue and a mercenary who was exposed to mustard gas during World War I. In search of a cure for the effects of the gas, Marcus discovered the Well of the Furies. He drank from the well and was granted incredible powers. Adopting the persona of Reichsman, Marcus used these powers in the service of the Axis powers on his world, leading them to victory over their foes. When he discovered the existence of another Earth, he traveled there and was defeated and imprisoned by the Freedom Phalanx. Now he's back, and ready for revenge."
// DisplayNames :
"P4106476151" "Reichsman"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Reichsman_H 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Reichsman_Invincible 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Reichsman_Cutscene 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_00001_Indestructable_Target 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3504022235" "Target Dummy"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fifth_Wolfpack_Boss_RomanEra 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Mueller 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P518904446" "Mueller has been a 5th Column sleeper agent, in place for years. He's just been waiting for his chance to help restore his beloved 5th Column to its rightful place. Now, with the return of Reichsman, the time is just right!"
// DisplayNames :
"P1954330914" "Roderick Mueller"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Power_Absorber 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2634137809" "Power Absorber"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Fifth_Mek_Man_Giant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P429434922" "Mek Man Gigantique"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_DeathField 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3124331725" "Death Field"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_FailSafe 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P772107918" "The Fail Safe device will destroy any follower of the Reichsman.  This is a last resort device."
// DisplayNames :
"P1774944184" "Fail Safe"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_5th_Empowerment_Alcove1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_5th_Empowerment_Alcove2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_5th_Empowerment_Alcove3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_5th_Empowerment_Alcove4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_5th_Empowerment_Alcove5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - 5thColumn_Protean 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P663448377" "Protean is a notorious shapeshifter, known for his murders of high profile heroes and their families. His earliest victims were the parents of Manticore. He also is responsible for the death of Dauntless, Galaxy Girl's sidekick. It was rumored that Manticore killed Protean in a fight some time ago but somehow Protean survived. He is now out to continue his reign of terror upon the people of Paragon and the Isles, while aiding the forces of Praetoria!"
// DisplayNames :
"P2677821990" "Protean"

