// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Eternal_Guard 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2131171953" "The Black Knights are an ancient Order of the dead that is charged with overseeing the Eternal Prison; a place where only the wickedest of souls are jailed. The Eternal Guards have sworn an oath to oversee the prison and to stand vigil over its twisted and varied denizens. Ranks of spear wielding Eternal Guards ensure that the walls never go unmanned and that evil is kept at bay."
// DisplayNames :
"P806265615" "Eternal Guard"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Black_Feather 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P309789873" "The Black Knights are an ancient Order of the dead that is charged with overseeing the Eternal Prison; a place where only the wickedest of souls are jailed. Black Feathers are said to shoot death on raven wings with their great bows, and indeed, their arrows are fletched with their namesake. With keen eyes, they watch for danger, ensuring that the walls of the Eternal Prison are never breached and that evil cannot escape."
// DisplayNames :
"P2896128697" "Black Feather"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Armiger 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2978947900" "The Black Knights are an ancient Order of the dead that is charged with overseeing the Eternal Prison; a place where only the wickedest of souls are jailed. Armigers are shield bearers that march at the forefront of the Black Knights when battle calls. Sworn to protect their sword brothers, they wade into battle without fear, relying on sturdy shield and heavy blade to carry the day. Every Armiger has sworn an oath to death before dishonor."
// DisplayNames :
"P4117714011" "Armiger"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Black_Chevalier 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2766341045" "The Black Knights are an ancient Order of the dead that is charged with overseeing the Eternal Prison; a place where only the wickedest of souls are jailed. Armed with great swords easily the height of most men, a Black Chevalier is an unstoppable force, bringing death and destruction in its wake. Where he walks, the foes of the Eternal Order fall in droves."
// DisplayNames :
"P2001082569" "Black Chevalier"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Dread_Templar 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1012958670" "The Black Knights are an ancient Order of the dead that is charged with overseeing the Eternal Prison; a place where only the wickedest of souls are jailed. Captains of the Eternal Order, the Dread Templars are amongst the oldest and most renowned of the knightly order. Few possess the dedication to become a Templar, but those that do are blessed with immense strength and resilience. Driven by their mighty oaths to the order, a Dread Templar will stop at nothing to vanquish their enemies."
// DisplayNames :
"P1534098817" "Dread Templar"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Black_Warden 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3438347822" "The Black Knights are an ancient Order of the dead that is charged with overseeing the Eternal Prison; a place where only the wickedest of souls are jailed. Black Wardens are the masters of the Eternal Prison, and form the inner circle of the Eternal Order. It is to them that the many and powerful oaths of the Black Knights are made, and it is solely upon them that the task of finding and punishing the souls of the wicked rests. Through powerful black spells the Black Wardens ensure that no soul can escape their grasp, and that the reward for a life of wickedness is bestowed upon those souls in the form of an eternity of agony from which there is no escape."
// DisplayNames :
"P1829044805" "Black Warden"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Scarlet 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P420962669" "Scarlet is a recent addition to the Black Knights and has proven herself a potent adversary through sheer determination and her fiery demeanor. Sir Agnan has taken her on as his squire in order to try and temper her aggressive disposition with a little wisdom and a lot of training."
// DisplayNames :
"P1786413001" "Scarlet"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Sir_Emric 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3532788841" "Of all the Black Knights, Sir Emric is the most beloved. Jovial and chivalric, Emric takes to battle with a mirth and flare that is often confused with madness."
// DisplayNames :
"P1887941228" "Sir Emric"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Sir_Bedwyr 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1867051459" "Sir Bedwyr is an exiled Black Knight who is seeking to discover and foil a plot by the Talons of Vengeance to destroy the Eternal Order of the Black Knights."
// DisplayNames :
"P3606008519" "Sir Bedwyr"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Sir_Agnan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3790769338" "Sir Agnan is one of the oldest and wisest of the Black Knights. Some say he was an old man when Lord Lorn first became Lord of the Eternal Prison. Whatever the truth is, Agnan's wisdom is to be respected. He has taken on the young warrior Scarlet as his new squire, and aims to teach her to temper her fighting spirit."
// DisplayNames :
"P1240356969" "Sir Agnan"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Lord_Lorn 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P720075700" "Lord Lorn is the Lord of the Eternal Prison and the first of the Black Knights. Under his watch none have ever escaped the Eternal Prison and he aims to keep it that way. He has arrived in Night Ward in pursuit of the Black Swan whose cruelty has earned her a place in Lorn's Eternal Prison, and he aims to collect her shortly."
// DisplayNames :
"P3682453843" "Lord Lorn"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Sir_Lucane 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3947558691" "Sir Lucane is an errant Black Knight who has sought out the Animus Arcana as potential allies against the Talons of Vengeance."
// DisplayNames :
"P2401845791" "Sir Lucane"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Black_Queen 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P900971464" "The Black Queen rules at the side of Lord Lorn and is normally in charge of the running of the Eternal Prison while Lorn is on campaign. She has come with her husband to Night Ward in search of the Black Swan, whose villainy has earned her a very special cage in the Black Queen's collection within the Eternal Prison. She is no stranger to warfare and weilds potent magic against any who dare raise a weapon against her."
// DisplayNames :
"P269989385" "Black Queen"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_P_Endgame_Pendragon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4201597175" "Born of death, the knight known only as Pendragon is the single mightiest combatant within the legion of the Black Knights.  No challenger has ever defeated him in single combat, and even the mighty Dread Templar whisper that some preternatural force guides Pendragon's every move.  Is he destined only to be Lorn's most potent blunt instrument?  Or is his past grander and his future greater than any around him have predicted?"
// DisplayNames :
"P2562500322" "Nega-Pendragon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Pendragon_EB 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1103316136" "Pendragon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Pendragon_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Tectonic_Assault 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2091714074" "Tectonic Assault"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_NetherPatch 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1650856938" "Nether Energy"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_DreadServant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1060058665" "Dread Servant"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Swords_Entity 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2396904871" "Swords Entity"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Swords_Target 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3332027955" "Swords Target"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Swords_Visual 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1799098832" "Swords Visual"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - BlackKnights_Swords_Damage 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2436746659" "Swords Damage"

