// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Guard 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2251411590" "Many who have lost hope go looking in dark places for the answers to life's questions. The Followers are those whose search has taken them to the Circle of Thorns. Now they must prove their true devotion by serving the Circle's evil will."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Guardian 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2638086659" "Guardian"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Archer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1057130050" "Archer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Defender 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2896300152" "Defender"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Guide 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P190834737" "Guide"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Wielder 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2931635028" "The mighty Thorn Wielders are the elite guardians of the Circle of Thorns. They wield the sacred Thorn Blades, enchanted weapons that leave a taint of foul magic on anyone they strike."
// DisplayNames :
"P3031096203" "Thorn Wielder"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Spectres 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2109280911" "The Circle's sunken city of Oranbega is rumored to be filled with the ancient ghosts of its original inhabitants. Some of these spirits become malevolent Specters, angry and incorporeal beings immune to physical attacks but capable of causing tremendous damage to living beings."
// DisplayNames :
"P3251578518" "Spectral Follower"
// DisplayNames :
"P3817440802" "Spectral Knight"
// DisplayNames :
"P1710094069" "Spectral Daemon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Spectres_Lords 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P648925503" "The Circle's sunken city is rumored to be filled with the ancient ghosts of its original inhabitants. Some of these spirits become malevolent Specters, angry and incorporeal beings immune to physical attacks but capable of causing tremendous damage to living beings."
// DisplayNames :
"P1477789683" "Spectral Daemon Lord"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Fire_Caster 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3665164771" "Weaving magical effects from fire can be dangerous for the novice mage, but Fire Casters have perfected the art. They can conjure up fires to immolate or distract their enemies, and some can even draw on their foes' body heat to restore their own power."
// DisplayNames :
"P1109339666" "Fire Thorn Caster"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Fire_Caster_Char 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Earth_Caster 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3196134264" "The Earth Casters' mastery over stone and sand makes them quite valuable in the underground city that the Circle of Thorns inhabits. But they can use their magic for more than digging tunnels and repairing walls. Under their control, the very ground beneath a hero's feet can become a deadly weapon."
// DisplayNames :
"P2505178718" "Earth Thorn Caster"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Earth_Caster_Prison 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Earth_Caster_Sand 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Air_Caster 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2182385436" "Air Casters can harness the winds to give themselves the power of flight. They can also conjure up meteorological menaces from lightning bolts to snow storms."
// DisplayNames :
"P1627131177" "Air Thorn Caster"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Air_Caster_Clap 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Air_Caster_Storm 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Ice_Caster 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P956684998" "The frigid magics of the Ice Casters take careful study to master. In the hands of these mages, ice becomes a deadly weapon, either shredding enemies with jagged blasts or freezing them in place and chilling them to their bones."
// DisplayNames :
"P2006940124" "Ice Thorn Caster"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Ice_Caster_Block 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Ice_Caster_Bitter 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_The_High_Life 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1492251934" "Magical mastery over life can be a powerful tool for good, but in the hands of the Life Mages it is a deadly weapon. They can suck the very life force out of their foes, weakening and eventually killing them."
// DisplayNames :
"P1469767263" "Life Mage"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_The_High_Energy 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P148964692" "Within their fabled lost city, the High Mages of Energy provide light, heat, and energy for their brethren. In battle they unleash their power in blasts of utter destruction, capable of ripping apart flesh, stone, and steel."
// DisplayNames :
"P1875192482" "Energy Mage"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_The_High_Force 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3632742419" "The High Mages of Force deal with the primal forces that move the universe. In their sunken city, they are responsible for preventing cave ins by siphoning off the Earth's seismic energy into useful pursuits. In battle, they can sap the very strength from a foe's limbs and add it to their own."
// DisplayNames :
"P153643484" "Force Mage"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_The_High_Soul 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P18704987" "The High Mages of the Soul delve into the deepest reaches of the human spirit. They are largely responsible for the gathering and training of specters and other spirits. When forced into combat, they petrify their foes in a wave of inescapable self-contemplation that leaves them incapable of any action."
// DisplayNames :
"P2478149091" "Soul Mage"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_The_Circle_Madness 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3689008004" "The Masters of Madness can control every aspect of the psyche. For their friends, they provide a constant aura of mental fortitude that helps them in all endeavors. In battle, their enemies suffer complete mental domination that leaves them incapable of any action at all."
// DisplayNames :
"P907918071" "Madness Mage"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_The_Circle_Madness_Low 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_The_Circle_Madness_High 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_The_Circle_Ruin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4269718102" "In ancient times, the Masters of Ruin could level whole cities with their powerful earthquake magic. Today these masters of mayhem are still deadly foes, capable of summoning localized tremors that cause great devastation in a short time."
// DisplayNames :
"P2214847474" "Ruin Mage"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_The_Circle_Agony 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3272048841" "There is not greater distraction than pain and suffering. The Masters of Agony often help relieve their friends of such distractions in times of peace. But when it comes to battle, they are adept at harming their foes through powerful and disruptive enchantments."
// DisplayNames :
"P2723239783" "Agony Mage"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_The_Circle_Death 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3975569745" "The most powerful of all the Circle's mages, the Masters of Death are lords of the afterlife. They help to wrangle and control the Behemoths and other beasts the Circle summons, but their most fearsome power is the ability to create a pervasive zone of death that sucks the life out of any foes in the vicinity."
// DisplayNames :
"P1948300329" "Death Mage"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Explosion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// GroupDescription :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Behemoth 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1159345437" "Summoned from the hellish pits of some other dimension, the Behemoths are fiery demons that inspire nightmares in all who see them. They can summon flaming swords to strike down their enemies, or breath fire from their mouths to incinerate all who stand before them."
// DisplayNames :
"P3768384234" "Behemoth"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Lt_Behemoth 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P417769902" "Behemoth Master"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Boss_Behemoth 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3820263025" "Behemoth Lord"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Lt_Behemoth_Lord 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2015898802" "The Behemoth Overlords are - fortunately - very rare. Likewise they are very deadly. Their mastery of fire allows them to immolate multiple foes simultaneously, and they can quickly heal their own wounds by basking in the heat of their infernal fire."
// DisplayNames :
"P1524953269" "Behemoth Overlord"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Boss_Behemoth_Lord 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Behemoth_Envoy 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P69856053" "Unbound and unnamed, it has crossed the gulf of worlds on a bridge of greed and pain. The Envoy of Shadow is the ambassador of the Prince of Demons, here to offer the Circle of Thorns great power and dark alliances. Its consuming flames and cloak of darkness are manifestations of its endless evil."
// DisplayNames :
"P2063063891" "Envoy of Shadow"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Baphomet 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1641554159" "The Baphomet is the oldest and most feared of the Behemoth Lords. The ground beneath its cloven feet burns with its own infernal fire."
// DisplayNames :
"P3985897732" "Baphomet"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Baphomet_Low 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Possessed_Scientists_Thorn_Fire_Caster 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4160056075" "The Circle of Thorns has possessed descendents of Mu for centuries, and has no intentions of stopping. Recently, they have begun possessing non-descendents for investigational purposes. When they discovered Portal Corporation's research, they began to possess employees to find a way to break their deal with the demonic brood. The Possessed Scientists have the powers of Thorn Casters, and are not afraid to use them."
// DisplayNames :
"P785497291" "Possessed Scientist"

