"P2533540291" "Hordeling Berserker"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_CoV_Boss_Hellstrike 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2038221951" "The deepest bowels of the Pit births these monstrosities. Beware their Infernal Blades, for it is said they tear far more than just flesh. Some claim bits of their victims souls are shorn away as well."
// DisplayNames :
"P4024240937" "Hellfrost"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_CoV_Elite_Boss_Lord 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2910058040" "These cruel demons command a host of dancing swords to flay the flesh of their foes."
// DisplayNames :
"P1840024338" "Blade Prince"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_CoV_Boss_Succubus 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3881738566" "Not every horror that emerges from the Inferno is hideous-at least on the outside. The Succubi appear as voluptuous women to lure foolish mortals to a long and painful doom."
// DisplayNames :
"P3705620092" "Succubus"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_CoV_Lilitu 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2955164023" "The She-Devil ruled some plane of Hell before being called forth by the Circle of Thorns. The sorcerers struck a deal with her, and Lilitu has come to Earth with her infernal hordes. It is said the price for her service is the death of 666 heroes - including her own son, Infernal."
// DisplayNames :
"P11599837" "Lilitu"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Dancing_Sword 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P210880508" "Dancing Infernal Sword"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_CoV_Nerva_Demon_Spectres 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1596061846" "Where go the Circle of Thorns go the legions of Hell. These gibbering monstrosities seem to be waiting for...something."
// DisplayNames :
"P4169677280" "Nerva Spectral Daemon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_CoV_Nerva_Demon_Spectres_Lords 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1422417101" "Nerva Spectral Daemon Lord"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_CoV_Caleb 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2694464209" "The legendary Caleb. You'd thought he was just a rumor-a tale told to frighten children by cruel parents. Yet here he is, brimming with infernal power and reeking of brimstone from the darkest depths of Hell."
// DisplayNames :
"P2685462576" "Caleb"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Circle_Mage_Archus 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2542197218" "Despite your efforts, Archus has nearly completed his psychic network using the shards of Seraphina's crystal. Stop him, or you could wind up as his pawn forever!"
// DisplayNames :
"P2085347683" "Circle Mage Archus"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Tree_Vine 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1870492773" "The vines of the Thorn tree can move and strike, cutting down those who would hurt its body. What's more, the main body of the tree cannot be attacked until all of the vines have been destroyed."
// DisplayNames :
"P784636496" "Thorn Tree Vine"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Thorn_Tree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1427803102" "A demon-tree of the netherworld, the Circle of Thorns use the Thorn Tree to siphon energy from an ancient fortress of the Mu. Unlike a normal plant, the Thorn Tree has its own defenses, and cannot even be damaged until the vines defending it have been cleared away."
// DisplayNames :
"P59076925" "Thorn Tree"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Baphomet_CoV 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Possessed_Mordrogar 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3917192417" "The Hellion known as Duke Mordragar has been possessed by the Circle of Thorns."
// DisplayNames :
"P1202169344" "Possessed Duke Mordorgar"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Akarist 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1517220836" "The ancient Oranbegan sorcerer known as Akarist was once a mortal man, over 14,000 years ago. In his original body, his magical powers were at their peak."
// DisplayNames :
"P1815807871" "Akarist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Arkus 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// GroupDescription :
"P1174607862" "Circle of Thorns"
// DisplayNames :
"P405018727" "Baron Zoria"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Rollister 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2821129019" "After performing the ritual for the Lance of Storms, Rollister's powers have increased ten fold! If he isn't stopped here, his power will become too much for anyone in Paragon to stop!"
// DisplayNames :
"P2560062409" "Rollister"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Diviner_Maros 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4261337083" "Diviner Maros is a figure of awe and terror, even among his fellow cultists within the Circle of Thorns. Though not the most powerful of their mystics, Maros has the ability or curse to see the past and future. Rumors say that his spirit was split across time after an accident during some arduous mystic research, but no one really knows the truth. Many within the Circle fear him, because his predictions come true all too often. When rumors arose that he was seeking freelancers to perform a tasks there was a great outcry within the Circle, but no one dared try to stop him."
// DisplayClassName :
"P274856297" "Seer"
// DisplayNames :
"P3553266623" "Diviner Maros"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - CircleOfThorns_Libri_Vermis 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3946202677" "Libri Vermis is the Circle of Thorns' foremost researcher and librarian. He has spent decades cataloging and reading the tomes within the vast libraries of the Circle of Thorns. He was the perfect choice to sequester the Malleus Mundi."
// DisplayNames :
"P427096682" "Libri Vermis"

