// Villain Def - Clockwork_Sprocket 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3968039773" "These pint-sized junkyard contraptions have become a real plague on the streets of certain neighborhoods. Their exact workings are mysterious, but there's no mystery about the deadly bolts of electricity they hurl at anyone who gets in their way."
// DisplayNames :
"P764994010" "Sprocket"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Summoned_Sprocket 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3157158168" "Cog"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Summoned_Sprocket_Babbage 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Summoned_Gears 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2121271238" "Gears emerge from the remnants of destroyed Clockwork Princes. Though tiny, they can still pack quite a punch."
// DisplayNames :
"P2876701861" "Gear"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Cog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Oscillator 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4055047761" "The airborne Clockwork Oscillators are a new and deadly threat to Paragon City's skies. Like their grounded counterparts, the Sprockets, these high-flying mechanical men attack using bolts of electricity. They are immune to any psychological attacks."
// DisplayNames :
"P1788816493" "Prototype Oscillator"
// DisplayNames :
"P4043541658" "Line Oscillator"
// DisplayNames :
"P1356920321" "Advanced Oscillator"
// DisplayNames :
"P2199979489" "Perfected Oscillator"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Lieutenant_Cannon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P66349415" "The Knights make up the bulk of the leadership class within the twisted court of the Clockwork King. Cannon Knights possess powerful, long range electrical attacks."
// DisplayNames :
"P1244255544" "Cannon Knight"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Lieutenant_Tesla 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2446746771" "The Knights make up the bulk of the leadership class within the twisted court of the Clockwork King. The Tesla Knights are especially dangerous because they enclose foes in deadly electrical cages."
// DisplayNames :
"P2744732369" "Tesla Knight"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Boss_Cannon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P707691266" "Like any monarch, the Clockwork King has his own court, although in his case it's composed of mechanical nobles called Dukes. These oversized robots are dangerous foes, possessing powerful long range electrical attacks."
// DisplayNames :
"P949253819" "Cannon Duke"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Boss_Tesla 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2966725418" "Like any monarch, the Clockwork King has his own court, although in his case it's composed of mechanical nobles called Dukes. The Tesla Dukes are dangerous foes, possessing the ability to imprison foes in crackling electrical cages."
// DisplayNames :
"P3569126364" "Tesla Duke"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Boss_Assembler 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3471452334" "Like any monarch, the Clockwork King has his own court, although in his case it's composed of mechanical nobles called Dukes. The Assembler Dukes can summon more Clockwork minions to their side during battle."
// DisplayNames :
"P177481604" "Assembler Duke"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Prince_Cannon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3766289191" "The heirs apparent to the Clockwork King's throne, the Princes represent the pinnacle of the mad genius' creations. Although Cannon Princes sometimes seem almost human because of their advanced robotic brains, they're still immune to mental attacks and can deal out massive electrical blasts."
// DisplayNames :
"P12427093" "Cannon Prince"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Prince_Cannon_Special 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Prince_Tesla 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P626674197" "The heirs apparent to the Clockwork King's throne, the Princes represent the pinnacle of the mad genius' creations. Although Tesla Princes sometimes seem almost human because of their advanced robotic brains, they possess the decidedly inhuman ability to imprison their foes in cages of electricity."
// DisplayNames :
"P3909943484" "Tesla Prince"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Prince_Assembler 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3412698777" "The heirs apparent to the Clockwork King's throne, the Princes represent the pinnacle of the mad genius' creations.  Assembler Princes' powerful electric attacks can blanket an area with painful lightning blasts. But it's their ability to rapidly produce more Clockwork soldiers that makes them truly insidious."
// DisplayNames :
"P1141892619" "Assembler Prince"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Lord 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2307643789" "These elite soldiers are the personal guard and right hand of the Clockwork King. You can be sure that they will stop at nothing to ensure his safety."
// DisplayNames :
"P1112468662" "Clockwork Lord"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Clockwork_King 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1113616968" "The mad Clockwork King imagines himself the center of a mechanical court. His powerful mind continually creates more subjects to his insane rule. The true horror is that his massive steel chassis holds a human brain."
// DisplayNames :
"P2758452314" "Clockwork King"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Babbage 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3107899879" "For reasons unknown, the Clockwork King created this giant automaton and loosed it upon Boomtown. Babbage seems chiefly interested in collecting metal scrap for its King, though it also fervently defends its territory from any hero incursions."
// DisplayNames :
"P2717693396" "Babbage"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Build_Paladin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1815480431" "What on earth are the Clockwork up to now.  This monstrosity must be destroyed!"
// DisplayNames :
"P484003428" "Clockwork Construction"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Clockwork_Paladin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2698845058" "The Clockwork have outdone themselves.  This Paladin of the Clockwork King must be destroyed!"
// DisplayNames :
